; The twins (docs/twins.md): the parts of the game that are made twice
; (src/game/Soldat_parts.mli), each done here with one of
; elm-playground's libraries, as a reader of that library's .mli would
; write it first. To teach, to compare with Soldat's own (src/orig),
; and to show the libraries at work in a whole game.
;
;   Soldat_engine_bot    the bots: Sense, Bot, Pathfind, Behavior (tiny_libs.ai)
;   Soldat_juice         the effects: Emitter, Trauma, Follow (tiny_libs.juice)
;   Soldat_bodies        how a thing falls: rigid bodies (the Playground's Physics)
;   Soldat_space         the sound's place: Space (tiny_libs.audio)
;   Soldat_lockstep      the network: two players, no server (Lockstep, Rollback)
;   Soldat_gui           the lobby's screen: the Playground's Gui
;   Soldat_twin          puts them in the game's slots (register)
;
; A program linked with this folder and not src/orig is the game on the
; Playground's libraries alone (mini-soldat-twin). Not counted in the
; budget (make loc). Pure OCaml.
(library
 (name soldat_twin)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries
   soldat_map soldat_assets soldat_game soldat_render soldat_net
   caps ; Cap.network: the authority to connect
   tiny_libs.core ; Basics
   tiny_libs.physics_2d ; Particles: a thing's points
   tiny_libs.ai ; Sense, Bot, Pathfind, Behavior
   tiny_libs.juice ; Emitter, Trauma, Follow
   tiny_libs.audio ; Space
   tiny_libs.networking_protocols ; Transport
   tiny_libs.networking_netcode ; Lockstep, Rollback, Checksum
   elm_playground)) ; Physics, Gui
